/* ===================== *
 *    Skullbreaker          *
 * ===================== */
@201 = ~skullbreaker~
@202 = ~Skullbreaker~
@203 = ~Skullbreaker:

The Skullbreaker is a brutal warrior trained to disable foes with blunt and spiked weapons. Each weapon in their arsenal delivers a distinct crippling effect, allowing the Skullbreaker to adapt to changing battles with crushing precision.

Advantages:
- Each time you hit an opponent with a blunt weapon, there is a 15% chance to apply an additional effect depending on the type of the equipped weapon:
  - Clubs: frighten the target for half a round
  - Maces: apply a -3 penalty to AC for 2 rounds
  - Flails/Morning Stars: cause a bleeding wound that continously deals damage over the next 3 rounds
  - War Hammers: briefly stun the target
  - Slings: briefly slow the target

Each effect may only be applied once per round to a single target and multiple application of the same effect do not stack.
However, different effects may be applied at the same time to a target.

- 2nd level: May use the Shockwave ability once per day, gains an additional use every 4 levels thereafter.

Shockwave:
All enemies within 15 feet are pushed back and stunned for half a round. Huge creatures are immune to the knockback effect.

- 10th level: Become immune to stun and knockback effects.
- 15th level: May use the Crushing Victory ability once per day.

Crushing Victory:
With every ounce of strength committed to a relentless assault, the Skullbreaker strikes with enough force to splinter shields and crush armor.
All crushing damage you deal within the next 5 rounds is doubled. 
Become winded after Crushing Victory ends, suffering a -2 penalty to AC and THAC0 as well as becoming fatigued.

Disadvantages:
- May only achieve Mastery (3 pips) in 1-handed blunt weapons and slings, all other weapons can only achieve proficiency.~

@204 = ~Shockwave~
@205 = ~Shockwave
All enemies within 15 feet are pushed back and stunned for 1 round. Huge creatures are immune to the knockback effect.~
@206 = ~Crushing Victory~
@207 = ~Crushing Victory:
With every ounce of strength committed to a relentless assault, the Skullbreaker strikes with enough force to splinter shields and crush armor.
All crushing damage you deal within the next 5 rounds is doubled.
Become winded after Crushing Victory ends, suffering a -2 penalty to AC and THAC0 as well as becoming fatigued.~
@208 = ~The Crushing Victory has ended and you are now winded.~